module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.refusal_decided_after_a_mutation

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data refusal_decided_after_a_mutation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "refusal_decided_after_a_mutation" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**a withholdable or fail-closed step that runs after a host mutation is a refusal after its effects** (INVALID STATE: a later command withholds or exits nonzero after a Mutate, so the host already holds the candidate binary, tree or unit when the apply fails. RECOGNITION RULE: the emit concatenates mutation commands, then a poison or a runtime fail-fast; a restart would start the new bytes under the still-loaded old claim.)",
    "FOUND AT (bright-moth-475, srv1:~/bm475-prod-apply-c22acb7-2026-10-12.log). NOT a poison: no __GUNBC_DEPLOY_REFUSED__. Cap WITHHELD is stderr line 471, an echo, HostScriptProceed. Outer: host_effect_apply shell exec exit=2. Last visudo stdout: /etc/sudoers.d/gunbc-approval-broker-helpers parsed OK. Last on-disk mutation that file 04:12:13; roadmap unit 04:09:19; NeedDaemonReload=yes (daemon-reload never ran). Nested gunbc was tree convergence (receipt 04:05:14), not the exit.",
    "FIXED IN THIS PR: each withholdable member producer returns Decide and Mutate from one case analysis of its own inputs; its refusal arm is a Decide fragment whose standing is HostScriptRefused, and its Mutate steps carry no poison. compose_host_script emits no Mutate when any Decide is HostScriptRefused (2026-09-17 withhold stays HostScriptProceed plus a CONVERGE_WITHHELD echo). Helper grant is installed before the roadmap unit dest, so a helpers-stretch failure no longer strands NeedDaemonReload. cmp without -s. compose prefixes __GUNBC_HOST_SCRIPT_STEP__ from each HostScriptFragment; apply frame exec 2>&1 so the next failure names its step on one stream even under bash -s. The cap member has a private _gunbc_cap_stage. ONE EXIT trap is parameterized by the stage vars the frame actually binds (apply: both; retract: _gunbc_stage only), so a successful retract no longer exits 1 under set -u after the mutations. That split is not the run-1 exit-2 cause. The memory-cap ordering gate is read once.",
    "IDENTIFIED CAUSE of the run-1 exit 2 (bright-moth-475, operator-local apply 2026-10-12 20:47, code-verified): approval_broker_helper_grant_admitted_steps installs the helpers readback at mode 0400 owned by fleet_posix_ci_runner_user (ghrunner). The next step, deploy_stage_cmp_stages_command, runs as the apply principal. Operator-local that is briansrls, which cannot read the file, so cmp exits 2. The 05:03 rerun passed only because the grant was already installed (Noop) and never reached the cmp. srv1-12 retirement was coincidental and is not the explanation. CapConvergeWithheld vs Authorized is not the leading reading. The shared _gunbc_stage hypothesis is withdrawn. The mode/owner mismatch is fixed in bright-moth-475's PR (number not opened yet); it is not fixed here.",
    "CONFIRMING EXPERIMENT, run (bright-moth-475, operator-local apply 2026-10-12 20:47): reproduced exit 2 at the helpers-readback cmp. Not a withheld-cap apply.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. CURRENT: mechanically preventable. Mutate still carries List of PipelineStep (authored strings), so a __GUNBC_*_REFUSED__ command remains writable there; no_member_mutate_steps_carry_a_refused_marker is the enrolled claim. The run-1 exit 2 is identified as the helpers-readback principal mismatch and is out of this PR. CEILING: structurally guaranteed once a silent fail-closed command cannot be authored in a Mutate. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER (Mutate poison): a Mutate step type that cannot carry a poison or an exit.",
    "TRAP DISCRIMINATORS ARE AD HOC, NOT ENROLLED. The retract-unbound-_gunbc_cap_stage class was executed in bash under set -euo pipefail (successful retract frame exit 0 and no leftover dir; two-dir trap with one var bound exit 1 leftover dir; apply frame exit 0 both dirs gone). Hermetic claims cannot execute a rendered script (shell.Exec.Run is wet / excluded). Those three frames are not a gunbc test label and not on the required witnesses path. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER (trap enrollment): a wet ProcessExit / bin_witness_wet that bash-executes those three frames.",
    "THE BASH ROUTE THE 2026-10-12 RECEIPTS DESCRIBE IS GONE, AND THE EVIDENCE NOW CITES ITS TYPED SUCCESSORS (2026-10-24). c11aa2317029 (#14660) deleted the bash apply: compose_host_script and its Decide/Mutate fragments, memory_cap_withheld_line, deploy_shell_merge_stderr_command and emit_release_member_effects; cb6548946213 (#14890) deleted the approval broker's helper grant, whose sudoers readback deploy_stage_cmp_stages_command compared; and the EXIT trap deploy_stage_dirs_exit_trap_command, left with no caller, is deleted with this receipt. Two of them have typed successors, and the evidence cites those: the refusal law of compose_host_script (no Mutate when any Decide refuses) is gunbc.live_deploy.apply_legs deploy_apply_chain (a refusal anywhere in the plan is the plan, so no leg is dispatched; enrolled as test.claim.live_deploy.live_deploy_apply_plan_witness a_refusal_ahead_of_planned_legs_yields_no_leg and a_refusal_after_planned_legs_drops_them_from_the_plan), computed in full before any port runs; the per-member Decide/Mutate production of emit_release_member_effects is deploy_apply_effects_plan; the withheld cap of memory_cap_withheld_line is deploy_apply_memory_cap_plan's CapAuthorizationWithheld arm, a report leg, never a refusal. The stderr merge, the stage-directory EXIT trap and the helpers-readback cmp have no successor, because the typed apply runs each leg as an argv with no shell frame and the helper grant no longer exists; those receipts record a route that is no longer on any path. The RUNG receipt above no longer holds: its CURRENT reading (mechanically preventable) rested on the enrolled claim no_member_mutate_steps_carry_a_refused_marker, which c11aa2317029 deleted with the script-text claims, and on a Mutate List of PipelineStep that no longer exists, so no executing evidence stands behind that reading. The successor witnesses named here exercise the plan-time refusal law, not the Mutate-poison class that rung was about, so they are not offered as holding it. The rung is not re-read here, and the row stays RungUnread.",
    "THE CAP AND SLICE-CONTROL FAMILIES LEFT THE INSTANCE APPLY (2026-10-30). The runner-unit caps and the slice control are host facts, and an instance apply carried them, so applying any instance on srv1 reconverged srv1's runner units through `systemctl revert`, which removed the srv1-02 role drop-in (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_residue_teardown_removes_every_dropin_of_the_unit_it_names). deploy_apply_memory_cap_plan, the cap member's private stage (deploy_cap_stage_dir_var) and its staged install (deploy_cap_upsert_staged_stmts) are deleted with them, so the withheld-cap successor named in the receipt above no longer exists and the evidence no longer cites it; the runner-unit caps are written by gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge alone, gated by gunbc.host.host_axis_caps cap_raise_standing; the cap authorization the instance apply consumed (cap_converge_decision and its target-unit roster) is deleted with it.",
    "SPECIMEN: THE EXIT DRAIN HANDED THE ATTEMPT'S OBLIGATION BEFORE IT CLAIMED THE ENTRY (srv1 lab, 2026-10-21). belt_exit_entry_drain_at decoded an exit record, ran enqueue (the effect: the obligation was handed to its unit) and only then moved the entry inbox -> queued. The move was the step that could refuse (a root-owned directory entry cannot be renamed by the service user), so the refusal was decided AFTER the mutation and the level-triggered path unit repeated the mutation: three obligation runs for one worker exit, each pass 6 minutes of CPU at an 8.1 GB peak. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the effect repeated; containment was by hand). REPAIR: CLAIM FIRST, the corpus's existing shape (belt_exit_entries_claim moves queued -> running before a run's first observation). The drain's only entry operation is the claim; belt_exit_queued_sweep_at, run in the same pass after the claims, is the sole hand-off, so a claim that fails has no effect to repeat (BeltExitEntryUnmovable). Hand-off latency does not grow: the sweep runs in the same pass as the claim. Behavior change: a refused enqueue no longer moves the entry to refused/ from the drain; it stays queued and the sweep retries it, exactly as it already did for a queued entry. RUNG AFTER REPAIR: mechanically preventable, for this site -- a discriminating RED (an unmovable entry hands nothing, and the enqueue count is stable across re-fired passes) is enrolled in test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_belt_exit_drain_wet_witness, and the invalid state (enqueue on the drain's claim path) is no longer writable there; the class stays at the rung of its weakest site. The sibling class is trigger_refires_on_a_nonempty_spool_whose_head_cannot_leave.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.apply_legs", decl_name: "deploy_apply_chain"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.apply_legs", decl_name: "deploy_apply_effects_plan"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.host_effect_realize", decl_name: "reconcile_shell_exec_observed"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_exit_entry_drain_at"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_exit_queued_sweep_at"),
  ],
}
